 "arc": "The shamrock variation: the free foot sweeps a clover arc across the floor while the supporting leg pivots under a quiet upper body. One cycle, captured slow (the source is about half this length), 3/4 view — the filmed view, not an instruction about the drawn character.\n\nFrames 0-5 stand over the character-left foot and settle to centre, the arms held low and quiet at waist height throughout; this step keeps its arms out of the way. Frame 6 is the fast pilot — the sweep itself, the one frame where the free leg travels. Frames 7-11 carry the weight onto the character-right foot with the character-left foot off the floor, frames 9 and 11 both reading as fast transitions rather than shapes to hold.\n\nFrame 12 puts the weight back onto the character-left foot and frames 13-15 return to centre, which is where frame 0 resumes. The seam is clean. Draw the arms as ballast: if they start gesturing, the footwork stops reading.",
